course: dictionary
lesson: 10457
title: Truthfully and honest talk
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Truthfully is an adverb. An adverb tells you how something is done, and truthfully means in an honest way, telling the truth. The noun is truth; truthfully describes how you speak or answer.
explain: Paul wrote, «speak truthfully to your neighbour», so he means we should be honest with the people around us. Ask yourself: speak how? The answer is truthfully. The word tells you the way to speak, with the truth and not with lies.
explain: Truthfully can also show that you are being honest about your own feelings. «Truthfully, I didn't like the film» tells you the speaker is admitting what they really think. «To be truthful» does the same job. When you meet a new word, check the words around it for clues.
fact: Truthfully means in an honest way, telling the truth.
fact: «Answer truthfully» means give a true answer, even when the true answer is hard to say.
fact: «Truthfully, I didn't like the film» means the speaker is being honest about their feelings.
fact: «To be truthful» and «truthfully speaking» introduce an honest opinion.
fact: In court, witnesses must answer truthfully.
exercise: Mia broke the vase. When Mum asked what happened, Mia answered truthfully. What did Mia do? | She blamed the cat | She hid the pieces under the bed | *She told Mum exactly what had happened
exercise: «Truthfully, I didn't like the film.» What does truthfully show? | The speaker is lying about the film | *The speaker is being honest about their feelings | The film was very long
exercise: Paul wrote, «speak truthfully to your neighbour.» What does truthfully describe? | The house where you live | *The way you speak | The time of day | The neighbour
test: Which word means in an honest way, telling the truth? | Barely | *Truthfully | Quickly | Loudly
test: What does «To be truthful, I forgot your birthday» show? | The speaker is late for school | *The speaker is admitting something honestly | The speaker is very happy
exam: Which sentence uses truthfully to show an honest opinion? | She ate the soup quickly | *Truthfully, the soup was too salty for me | He spilled the soup on the floor | The soup was hot and steaming
